{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1354844-trader-of-wonders","id":1354844,"title":"Trader of Wonders:","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-13T18:33:07-08:00","id":1354844,"title":"Trader of Wonders:","content":"Liu Vess was Exalted by the god of a river. Among his powers, the most apparent is the ability to sail his ship, <i>Resolute</i>, by all appearances a blue-water merchant vessel, through waters too narrow or shallow for it. He is almost always seen sailing the ship up or down the river. Other than him, the crew of the ship typically consists of 30 ghosts, who he has found haunting locales he visited on his travels. His Defining Intimacy is a desire to help and protect the people who live near this river. He prefers not to accomplish this by fighting directly, but by trading valuable goods such as artifacts, secrets, favors, and opportunities for adventure with powerful individuals he meets on his travel. He usually has a few artifacts on the <i>Resolute</i> at any given time, with a greater number of ordinary rarities, but the majority of his cargo space is usually filled with grain and other basic necessities which he trades for a fair price to the poorer people in villages along the river. He is typically seen at the prow of his ship, and rarely leaves it, even when conversing with those on the ground. He rarely fights except in self-defense, but when forced to protect himself or the <i>Resolute</i> are attacked, he uses a bow and arrow.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence:</b> 2, <b>Willpower:</b> 5, <b>Join Battle</b>: 6<br /> <b>Personal motes:</b> 14, <b>Peripheral Motes:</b> 33 (11 committed at most times<br /> <b>Health Levels: </b>-0/-1x2/-2x2/-4/Incap. <br /> <b>Attributes</b><br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2, Charisma 2, Manipulation 3, Appearance 2, Perception 4, Intelligence 4, Wits 3<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b><br /> Archery 3, Athletics 1, Awareness 3, Bureacracy 4, Dodge 3, Integrity 2, Investigation 3, Linguistics 1, Lore 3, Occult 3, Presence 3, Resistance 2, Sail 4, Socialize 2<br /> <br /> <b>Combat</b><br /> Attack (longbow) 6 dice (+accuracy modifier), 9 damage<br /> Combat movement 6 dice<br /> Evasion 3, Parry 1<br /> Soak/Hardness 5/0 (chain shirt)<br /> <br /> <i>Powers</i><br /> <br /> <b>Excellencies</b>: Liu Vess may add up to (Ability) dice to an action with his excellency. When on a ship he commands, this is increased to (Attribute + Ability).<br /> <br /> <i>Combat Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Spring River\u2019s Bounty</b> (4m; supplemental): This charm supplements an Archery attack. Once shot, the arrow splits in two, with both arrows aiming towards the same target. Liu Vess makes two attack rolls, with excellencies and other charms counting for each, and then chooses one (usually the highest). On a decisive attack, if both attacks would hit, Liu Vess gains 2 initiative after resetting to base initiative.<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn River\u2019s Fog</b> (5m; reflexive; until next term): Liu Vess is surrounded by mist, which he seems to blend into, making his location unclear to enemies. He ignores wound and onslaught penalties to his Evasion until his next turn, and gains 1 initiative for each attack he succesfully evades.<br /> <br /> <i>Sailing charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Not Trouble Still Water</b> (Xm; pilot; indefinite): This charm allows Liu Vess to sail a ship in waters that would ordinarily be too shallow for it. The ship is seemingly supported by a mysterious force, and sails as if in a much deeper body of water. Dangers in the water harm the ship as normal, but it is always possible to roll to avoid a danger if a boat of any size could. During non-emergency situations, the ship can maneuver around other ships in the water with ease - a light fog is sometimes created to conceal exactly what is happening - and in an emergency situation, a suitable Sail roll will avoid a collision. This requires committing a number of motes equal to the maximum hull level of the piloted ship.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Ship Method</b> (Xm; indefinite): This charm allows restless shades to take physical form sufficient to serve as the crew of a ship, even if they would not normally have human-like intelligence or be able to take physical form. It costs 1 mote for each 5 ghosts enhanced this way. The simplest spirits may perform all basic nautical tasks while stronger ghosts can perform any task other than piloting the ship. With an appropriate crew of ghosts, the pilot does not take penalties for having an inexperienced crew, and if a majority of the ghosts were skilled sailors in life, gains the bonus for having a crew of skilled sailors. The ghosts find this a pleasant experience, with the Essence conferring a slight feeling of being alive, or being part of a larger living organism, and granting a taste of Liu Vess\u2019s emotions, but are not compelled to sail the ship - finding a suitable crew of ghosts is its own task. They can turn immaterial when threatened but otherwise are ineffective in hand-to-hand combat. Mortals, and stranger creatures, may join the crew, but find it difficult to communicate with the ghosts unless they have relevant abilities, as the ghosts rarely speak and speak in strange words when they do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Social charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mystical Merchant\u2019s Eye</b> (4m; simple; instant and \u2014; permanent): By succeeding at a (Perception + Bureaucracy) Read Intentions action against a target\u2019s Guile, Liu Vess learns which of the artifacts, secrets, and other treasures in his possession the target might particularly value, and roughly what they value them for. This confers one bonus success on later rolls to bargain over these items with the target, but it is not sufficient to obviate the need for bargaining. It does not reduce the risk of being cheated, except by those who value the items greater than their own ability to pay, a fact which is revealed by a successful roll. This charm also has a passive form - on merely looking at someone who is wealthy or powerful enough to make a fair trade for such goods, but whose appearance does not reveal this fact, Liu Vess can make a roll of the same type to intuit it. Boosting one\u2019s Guile against this roll automatically boosts it against the active use of the charm if it follows within the same Scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Secret-Hungry Gaze</b> (2m; reflexive; instant): If another character offers to share a secret or other valuable information with Liu Vess, he can determine the importance and value of the information, and if they really hold it, from a brief description of it. After agreeing to a trade for the information, and receiving it, he can tell if he was lied to or if the character gave him the information to the best of their knowledge. This defeats all non-magical attempts to deceive him on this matter and forces defeats magical deception after a successful opposed (Perception + Bureaucracy) roll, with double 9s.<br /> <br /> <b>Frozen Winter River</b> (3m; reflexive; scene): Liu Fess\u2019s Resolve and Guile are each increased by 1 for a scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Resources</i><br /> <br /> <b>Resolute </b><br /> <b>Role: </b>Rivergoing merchant vessel <br /> <b>Speed: </b>Current +1; sail +2; empty cargo hold +1 <br /> <b>Maneuverability: </b>+0; <b>Hull: </b>-1/-1/-2/-4/Incapacitated <br /> <b>Cargo: </b>2,000 tons or more. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}